# Rust build artifacts. Since hwprivacy-lsm joined the workspace, ALL crates
# build into this one shared directory — hwprivacy-lsm/target/ no longer exists
# and must not come back, or scripts pointing at the old path silently run a
# frozen binary. That happened on 2026-08-05.
target/
hwprivacy-lsm/target/

# Generated from the RUNNING kernel's BTF by the Phase 0 toolchain script.
# Machine- and kernel-specific, 2.6 MB, regenerate with:
#   bpftool btf dump file /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux format c > src/bpf/vmlinux.h
hwprivacy-lsm/src/bpf/vmlinux.h

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# python bytecode from tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
target/openprobe

# Stray ImageMagick dump, committed by accident 2026-09-01 (187 MB).
sys

# Internal working files — kept locally, not published.
#
# These are the working surface between Costin and Claude, not product docs:
# CLAUDE.md and HANDOFF.md are session state, claude-memory.md is an
# auto-generated mirror of what Claude remembers, LOG.md is an append-only
# record of when work happened, and the .code-workspace carries local paths.
# Excluded on publication 2026-09-06. The docs-yaml/ ADRs stay published —
# they are engineering documentation and stand on their own.
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md
LOG.md
hwprivacy.code-workspace
docs-yaml/claude-memory.md
